TITLE:Delay Check
SUBTITLE:--Positive, negative and overlapping #DELAY against a click track
GENRE:Test Charts
BPM:120
WAVE:click.ogg
OFFSET:0
DEMOSTART:0

// The audio clicks every beat (0.5 s), high on each bar line; a measure is 2 s.
// Every section starts on a bar line and is followed by an empty measure.
COURSE:Easy
LEVEL:1
BALLOON:4
#START
0,
// 1. Baseline: four Don on the clicks.
1111,
0,
// 2. PeepoDrumKit +16 ms note offset (#DELAY x before the note, #DELAY 0 after it).
// #DELAY adds up, so from the 2nd Don on everything stays 16 ms late.
1
#DELAY 0.016
1
#DELAY 0
11,
0,
// 3. PeepoDrumKit -16 ms: back on the clicks from the 2nd Don on. Failed to load before 2026-10-02.
1
#DELAY -0.016
1
#DELAY 0
11,
0,
// 4. Ka half a beat late, then put back: Don, Ka between clicks 2 and 3, Don, Don.
1
#DELAY 0.25
2
#DELAY -0.25
11,
0,
// 5. Ka half a beat early: Don, Ka between clicks 1 and 2, Don, Don.
1
#DELAY -0.25
2
#DELAY 0.25
11,
0,
// 6. Out of file order: the Ka is written after the first Don but lands half a beat before the bar line.
1
#DELAY -0.75
2
#DELAY 0.75
11,
0,
// 7. Two measures overlap: big Don, big Ka, big Don, big Ka on clicks 3 to 6 of the pair.
#DELAY 1
3030,
#DELAY -1.5
4040,
#DELAY 0.5
0,
// 8. Roll stretched by half a beat: it ends on the next bar line.
50
#DELAY 0.5
08,
#DELAY -0.5
0,
// 9. Balloon (4 hits) cut short by a negative delay: it ends 1.5 beats after it starts.
70
#DELAY -0.75
08,
#DELAY 0.75
0,
// 10. Go-Go at 240 BPM: four Don on 16ths, then four Ka a 32nd late.
#GOGOSTART
#BPMCHANGE 240
1111
#DELAY 0.0625
2222,
#DELAY -0.0625
0,
#BPMCHANGE 120
#GOGOEND
0,
// 11. A #SCROLL 0.5 that a negative delay moves before the #SCROLL 2: the later command wins,
// so the whole measure scrolls at half speed.
#SCROLL 2
1
#DELAY -1
#SCROLL 0.5
#DELAY 1
111,
#SCROLL 1
0,
0,
#END
